        <div class="prose">
          <h2>Our purpose</h2>
          <p>RallyGood is being established to relieve poverty and urgent practical need for people anywhere in the world, by funding essential goods and services such as shelter, food, clean water, hygiene products and warmth, and to support community wellbeing through access to nature.</p>
          <p>We do this by raising money for specific appeals, called Drops, and working through verified local partner organisations. For every Drop we aim to publish evidence and a close-out report so supporters can see how their contribution was used.</p>
          <h2>Local, nature-based wellbeing</h2>
          <p>Our purposes also include supporting community wellbeing and social inclusion through access to nature-based and other programmes for people experiencing disadvantage, isolation or barriers to participation, in the UK and overseas. This includes forest bathing. We plan to run some programmes ourselves with trained facilitators and to fund partner organisations to run others. Access is intended to be free, with an optional suggested donation and no one excluded if they cannot or do not wish to give. <a class="text-link" href="nature-wellbeing.html">Read more about our nature and wellbeing work</a>.</p>
          <h2>Where we are</h2>
          <p>RallyGood is being set up as a charitable incorporated organisation (CIO) with trustees. <strong>Charity registration is pending</strong>, and we are not yet accepting donations. We will not describe ourselves as a registered charity until registration is complete.</p>
          <h2>What we are – and are not</h2>
          <p>We are a fundraising and verification layer: we mobilise supporters, check partners and costs, move funds under clear controls and report back. We are not an emergency first-response organisation, and we do not claim to have trained response teams or logistics of our own.</p>
          <p>By default we raise funds in the UK and buy locally or regionally through partners, rather than collecting and shipping goods.</p>
        </div>
